{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1087", "sample_idx": 29, "model_name": "abacusai/dracarys-llama-3.1-70b-instruct", "content": "the social network is a biographical drama film directed by david fincher, based on the life of mark zuckerberg, the co-founder and ceo of facebook. the movie is written by aaron sorkin, who is known for his witty and fast-paced dialogue. the film stars jesse eisenberg as mark zuckerberg, andrew garfield as eduardo saverin, and justin timberlake as sean parker.\n\nthe movie starts with mark zuckerberg, a sophomore at harvard university, who is dumped by his girlfriend erica albright (played by rooney mara). mark, who is a computer science major, decides to create a website called \"facemash\" that allows users to compare the photos of two students and vote on which one is more attractive. the site becomes a huge success, but also gets mark into trouble with the university administration.\n\nmark is approached by cameron and tyler winklevoss (played by armie hammer), who are members of the rowing team, to create a social networking site exclusively for harvard students. mark agrees to work on the project, but eventually drops it to work on his own idea, which becomes facebook.\n\nmark teams up with his best friend eduardo saverin, who provides the initial funding for the site. facebook quickly becomes a huge success, and mark becomes a celebrity on campus. however, mark's relationship with eduardo deteriorates, and eduardo eventually sues mark for diluting his shares in the company.\n\nmeanwhile, mark meets sean parker, the co-founder of napster, who becomes a mentor to mark and helps him to expand facebook. sean's influence on mark leads to a rift between mark and eduardo, and the two friends eventually part ways.\n\nthe movie ends with mark's deposition, where he is being sued by eduardo and the winklevoss twins. mark is shown to be a complex character, who is both brilliant and socially awkward. the movie raises questions about the true nature of mark's intentions and the consequences of his actions.\n\noverall, the social network is a well-crafted movie that explores the complexities of mark zuckerberg's character and the early days of facebook. the movie features excellent performances from the cast, particularly jesse eisenberg, who brings mark's character to life. the film's direction and cinematography are also noteworthy, with david fincher using a dark and moody tone to convey the intensity of the story.\n\nthe movie's score, composed by trent reznor and atticus ross, is also worth mentioning. the music is a perfect blend of electronic and orchestral elements, and it adds to the overall tension and drama of the film.\n\nin conclusion, the social network is a must-see movie for anyone interested in the story of facebook and mark zuckerberg. it is a thought-provoking film that raises important questions about the consequences of success and the nature of friendship.", "logprobs": [{"token": "the", "logprob": -0.11627468466758728}, {"token": " social", "logprob": -1.6927862816373818e-05}, {"token": " network", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.03940728306770325}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -1.3828373084834311e-05}, {"token": " bi", "logprob": -2.3928215503692627}, {"token": "ographical", "logprob": -1.1920930376163597e-07}, {"token": " drama", "logprob": -5.245222382654902e-06}, {"token": " film", "logprob": -0.0008272373233921826}, {"token": " directed", "logprob": -0.4379572570323944}, {"token": " by", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " david", "logprob": -3.576279254957626e-07}, {"token": " fin", "logprob": -1.1920930376163597e-07}, {"token": "cher", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.6935621500015259}, {"token": " based", "logprob": -0.37821662425994873}, {"token": " on", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.00017924723215401173}, {"token": " life", "logprob": -1.4605791568756104}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.0005950313643552363}, {"token": " mark", "logp